From 829444b5e8413fc7db8511b2aec91ab7af37d4fe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ananya Sridhar <ananyasridhar108@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 04:03:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Kid login flow: real illustrated creatures instead of emoji,
 warm up the sterile card UI
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The page a kid lands on right after tapping 'I'm a Kid!' on Landing, before
they ever reach the game list, was the coldest screen in the whole app: a
flat two-stop navy gradient, a single generic controller emoji floating in
a blurred circle, and a plain bg-brand-card square for the actual
register/login form — visually disconnected from Landing's illustrated
dusk-and-ember world one screen earlier, and from GamePicker one screen
later.

- components/ui/Creatures.jsx (new): six hand-drawn-style SVG creatures
  (Chicky, Dino, Cloudy, Starry, Zoom, Finley) replacing the flat
  emoji-in-a-gradient-circle Avatar, in the same gradient-body/dot-eyes/
  blush-cheeks language as Landing.jsx's existing BreathBuddy illustration.
  Gradient ids are namespaced per-instance via useId() — GamePicker renders
  the same avatar twice on one page (header + hero), which would otherwise
  silently collide on a shared linearGradient id.

- components/ui/index.jsx: Avatar now renders a Creature instead of an
  emoji span. This is the shared component used by Landing, GamePicker,
  GameNavbar, both dashboards, MyProgress, and PatientDetail, so the fix
  cascades everywhere avatars appear, not just this one page.

- pages/kid/Play.jsx: carried Landing's dusk-into-ember gradient and ember
  particles through instead of dropping into a flat navy square; replaced
  the lone floating game-controller emoji with a small floating "welcome
  crew" of three creatures; replaced the flat card with a gradient-bordered
  glass panel matching Landing's existing button treatment; swapped every
  remaining decorative emoji for lucide icons or the creatures themselves.

Caught and fixed a real bug before committing: GlassPanel's border color
was originally written using a CSS custom property the app's Tailwind v3
setup never generates, so it would have silently fallen through to
currentColor on every panel, matching no accent color at all. Replaced
with an explicit accent-to-hex map.

Verified: npm run build succeeds clean (643 modules, no errors) both
before and after the GlassPanel fix; oxlint clean across the whole
frontend (0 errors, only 2 pre-existing-style fast-refresh warnings on
Creatures.jsx's data exports — the only warnings in the repo, both mine,
both harmless/dev-only); scripted a Unicode-range scan of Play.jsx
confirming zero emoji characters remain (the backspace-key glyph on the
PIN pad is a keyboard symbol, U+232B, deliberately left as-is, not an
emoji); diffed the shared Avatar change line by line. Could not get a
real rendered screenshot — this sandbox can't keep a backgrounded vite
dev server alive across tool calls — so this is verified by build/lint/
diff, not by eye; worth a visual pass in a real browser before
considering it fully done.
